; ==========================================================================
; STELLAR GETTING WARMER  -  guess the number from 1 to 1000   (loads at $4000)
; ==========================================================================
; Load, cold-boot, press any key. Type a guess and Enter; you are told to go
; higher or lower and, from the second guess on, whether you are getting
; warmer or colder than your last guess. Ten guesses - always enough if you
; halve the range each time. Anything that is not a number from 1 to 1000
; does not use a guess; Q gives up. Y plays again, N quits.
;
; Plain text - no VT100 codes needed.
;
; VERIFICATION (Firmware-Math/warmer_verify.py, V0061.34): PASS 2026-10-01 - 456 games, every byte of the transcript matched a Python model: 300 halving games (all won in <= 10; numbers 3..997), 150 random players with junk lines and Q, edges (1, 1000, first-guess win, backspace, ten-guess loss), rerun from dirty RAM.
; HW-VERIFIED on the Elf2K (V0061.34), 2026-10-01 - Craig: "Getting Warmer works."
;
; 222 STELLAR commands.
;
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DISASSEMBLY  -  commented out; the loader skips it
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

; D 4000 CD             START
; D 4001 11 0F 00 0A    LOADXI R15 000A                    Ten
; D 4005 11 0B 00 00    LOADXI R11 0000                    RB = 0: the index for writing variables
; D 4009 10 00 00       LOADAI 0000
; D 400C 2F 0B 07 8C    WRITEIDX R11 078C                  NBUF ends in a 0
